title: 'Git discovery uses the raw wiki_root: the git option silently turns off for
  a root given as ~/…'
updated: 2026-11-03T19:27:47Z
---

Found by p5-mcp-hub's k29 research. Pages are served from '~/wiki' (Path::Tiny expands ~), but MCP::Wiki::Git::History calls Git::Raw::Repository->discover($self->wiki_root) (lib/MCP/Wiki/Git/History.pm:54) with the literal string, so discovery fails and history/auto-commit are silently off with --git. Discover from the resolved path.

From p5-mcp-hub (k37 design, 2026-11-03): mcp-hub passes class args unexpanded, so any hub config written with '~/wiki' silently loses git history. Hub users hit this directly — worth a higher priority.
